# Fault J-D-1: a hole movement (fee_out[2026-07], amount the hole fee_amt[2026]) fulfilled by an observation still
# printed the hole. L §5.19 Realised amounts: "An observation that fulfils a hole movement answers it: its day and
# amounts are the instance's"; E §4.1 step 3: an instance "fulfilled by an observation the cut sees, which stands in
# for it" is modelled past. flows of fee_out over July is the observation's 5.00 PLN; over August, the hole (q).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source own "own"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input bank: observed
input dom: int
input fee_amt[y in years]: money PLN question "fee?"
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
move fee_out[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to world amount fee_amt[year_of(m)]
ask q: flows(fee_out, 2026-07), flows(fee_out, 2026-08)
version v
  cite own
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  dom = 7 "own"
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "o"
version b
  cite own
  known 2026-07-08
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-07-07, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to world amount 5.00 PLN, fulfils: fee_out[2026-07]) "x"
=== expect
q: (5.00 PLN, ?"fee?" (fee_amt[2026]))
  unfulfilled: fee_out[2026-08]
  cut 2026-10-20
